# MS-161 Phase D — LeakSanitizer suppressions for the OPTIONAL MATRIX_MLX_INPROC
# coordinator build, which embeds CPython (libpython3.12) + mlx_lm.
#
# The default/shipped coordinator is pure C++ (no CPython) and runs ASan clean
# with NO suppressions — these are only needed when running the in-process
# (MATRIX_MLX_INPROC=1) build under a sanitizer that supports LeakSanitizer.
#
# NOTE: LeakSanitizer is NOT available on macOS arm64. This file is for Linux
# sanitizer runs of the in-process build, or future CI. On macOS, AddressSanitizer
# (use-after-free / overflow detection) works without it.
#
# Usage:
#   MATRIX_SANITIZE=address MATRIX_MLX_INPROC=1 bash scripts/build_cpp_binaries.sh
#   LSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=scripts/asan_python.supp ./coordinator
#
# CPython's small-object allocator (pymalloc) and one-time interpreter state
# are intentionally not freed before process exit — these are not real leaks.
leak:_PyObject_Malloc
leak:_PyMem_RawMalloc
leak:PyMem_RawMalloc
leak:_PyRuntimeState_Init
leak:Py_InitializeFromConfig
leak:PyImport_ImportModule
leak:_PyRuntime
# mlx_lm / mlx Python extension one-time module + Metal device init
leak:mlx
leak:libmlx
